# Keep the build context to the application itself.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` swept the whole backend directory into the
# image: a 180MB Windows virtualenv that a Linux container can never use, the
# runtime state directories, and — the reason this file is not merely an
# optimisation — `.env`, which put every secret into an image pushed to a
# registry.
#
# NOT excluded, deliberately: config/metadata (the published semantic layers
# must ship in the image), sql/, and Pipfile/Pipfile.lock.

# Secrets. Local runs read .env from the HOST via docker-compose's `env_file`,
# and deployments inject the environment through Portainer, so nothing needs
# it inside the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p8

# Virtualenvs — built for the host OS, wrong architecture, and reinstalled by
# `pipenv install --system` during the build anyway.
.venv
venv
ENV

# Runtime state, written by the running app. Shipping it means one user's
# sessions and another's chat history travel inside the image.
.conversations
.sessions
excel_storage
excel_inbox

# Python build artefacts
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# Local noise
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
*.log
.DS_Store
